# Path B: the Caddy that ALREADY runs on the server (for the other site)
# also serves Salio. Installed by the commands in deploy/DEPLOY.md
# ("Path B: add Salio to the server's Caddy"), which copy this file and
# salio-rules.caddy to /etc/caddy/sites/, replace SALIO_DOMAIN_GOES_HERE
# with SALIO_DOMAIN from .env, and add one line to the main Caddyfile:
#   import /etc/caddy/sites/salio-host.caddy
#
# It names only Salio's own hostname, so it cannot take requests meant for
# the other site. The two ports are SALIO_API_PORT and SALIO_WEB_PORT in
# .env (127.0.0.1 only).
#
# The rules themselves are in salio-rules.caddy, shared with Path A.

import salio-rules.caddy

SALIO_DOMAIN_GOES_HERE {
	import salio_site 127.0.0.1:18080 127.0.0.1:18081
}
